    "title": "On looking and Ledger: Brokeback Mountain at 20",
    "text": "Jake Gyllenhaal and Heath Ledger – Brokeback Mountain – 2005 (Focus/Kobal/Shutterstock) Brokeback Mountain was released 20 years old today, another “where did the time go?” checkpoint for elder Millennials. But Brokeback Mountain marks time in a unique and culturally important way, as it is one of the major turning points in queer pop culture, when queer cinema took a big step into the mainstream.\nOf course, today Brokeback Mountain would be made by a queer filmmaker and star at least one out actor, but today’s Hollywood is built on the evolutions of what came before, and in 2005, the idea of two of the hottest young working actors – one already an established romantic lead – playing gay cowboys in an explicit queer romance positioned as a major film during awards season was, truly, a seismic shift…\nSource link",
